    "created_at": "2026-11-06T23:56:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-06T23:56:02Z",
    "body": "Fixed (staged, uncommitted; main reviews/commits). Cause: a whole-part (Entity) source under Pocket / 2D Adaptive / 2D Offset built its region from the part's own section at Top Z (`source_region`), so the pocket hollowed the part. Fix: `area::whole_model_pocket` / `around_part`. With a setup stock, a whole-part source now clears the stock silhouette minus every part section standing at the ladder planes (the same island law `pocket_region_on_part` uses, factored into `minus_standing`). It is wired into the job precompute (job.rs) and the preview (material_region.rs), and works under a 3+2 tilt (in local frame). A part that fills the stock outline is refused by name. A Stock source, or a model with no stock, keeps the documented 'volume to remove' reading. Pinned by crates/app/tests/whole_model_pocket.rs: `a_whole_part_pocket_clears_the_stock_around_the_part_never_its_section`, `a_whole_part_adaptive_clears_the_stock_around_the_part_never_its_section`, `a_whole_part_pocket_whose_part_fills_the_stock_is_refused_by_name`. Separate defect found (not fixed here): 2D Adaptive's HSM plan rounds an island's convex corner 0.30 mm inside the tool radius and verify reports clean. It is pinned by the ignored test `a_whole_part_adaptive_keeps_the_full_tool_radius_off_the_part` and needs its own issue.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
